# review-mounted.txtar
#
# testscript: executable
#
# `cascade review` mount proof (P1-E25-W5-S52-T5 REWORK fix, BLOCK 1). The
# adversarial review's own reproduction was exactly this: `cascade --help`
# never listed `review`, and `cascade review --diff x --level A` exited 2
# with "unknown flag: --diff" -- cobra treating "review" as an unmatched
# arg to root, not a subcommand, because nothing had called
# root.AddCommand on it. Run in process by TestScript (script_test.go)
# against the REAL newRootCmd() tree -- the same composition the shipped
# binary builds (root.go's mountSubcommands calls mountReviewCmd,
# cmd/cascade/review_mount.go) -- so what this proves is what an
# operator's own shell would see, not a synthetic tree built only for a
# test.
#
# SCOPE: only the two assertions that hold regardless of which
# provider.ReviewProvider is currently installed live here -- this
# driver's own directive set (env/exec/stdout/stderr, script_test.go) has
# no hook to swap plugins/review's package-level reviewProvider seam
# around one exec line, and by the time this test runs, root.go's real
# import chain (internal/plugins, transitively, via builtin_plugins.go)
# has already wired the REAL provider, which would try to dial a daemon
# socket this test environment does not have. The "exits 0 with findings"
# and "an unconfigured provider refuses" assertions D2 also names live in
# review_mount_test.go instead, where SetReviewProvider can be swapped
# deterministically before each exec.

# The noun is mounted: --help reaches cmd.go's real Long/flag surface,
# not root's own "unknown command" refusal.
exec cascade review --help
stdout 'native adversarial reviewer'
stdout '--diff'
stdout '--pr'
stdout '--level'
stdout '--json'

# No --diff or --pr: the real validateReviewFlags refusal (KindInvalidInput
# text), not cobra's own unmatched-arg error -- proving dispatch reaches
# cmd.go's RunE, not merely that help text renders.
! exec cascade review
stderr 'one of --diff or --pr is required'

# --diff and --pr together: the same validator's other branch.
! exec cascade review --diff x --pr y
stderr '--diff and --pr are mutually exclusive'

# A stray positional argument is refused (cobra.NoArgs), same as every
# other mounted command's guardUnknownSubcommands/Args discipline.
! exec cascade review extra-arg
stderr 'unknown command'
